30,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My findings suggest a shift in our human landscape. We have plenty of interest in digital roles, but our experienced phenotyping technicians have largely vanished.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Oh! I found out that shipping costs are going up, but the government is still helping with glasshouse fees. Also, computing is free, but animal costs are way higher!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The records are... discouraging. Catalogue projects last for years, but the ones trying to prove a specific mechanism often end without an answer.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"It's a mess. Field sites are getting hit by fires and floods, and the spectroscopy suite was broken for eleven weeks because of a contract!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The repository is finally fast, which is good. But the glasshouses are completely full for the next two cycles. We can't put anything more in there.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Minako, that is a critical constraint. If the glasshouses are full, any project relying on them will be stalled before it begins.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Minako, wait, if they're full, does that mean the subsidy I saw doesn't even matter? That's so silly!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, if the technicians are gone, then even the ""safe"" projects might fail if they need specialized hands for phenotyping.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"Exactly! And if the equipment is breaking and the field sites are flooding, we're just gambling with the grant money.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Takumi, the infrastructure is strained. We cannot afford a project that adds more pressure to the glasshouses or relies on fragile instrumentation.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Servas,,It seems we are uncovering a pattern of fragility. We must find a path that avoids these systemic frictions to protect the researchers.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Sakura,,I just want to make sure whoever we pick doesn't end up paying for expensive shipping out of their own pocket!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I agree with Servas. We should prioritize projects that provide lasting utility—like catalogues—rather than risky mechanism studies.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Takumi,,I'm with Daisuke. No more gambling. We need something that doesn't depend on a broken spectroscopy suite or a flooded field.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We are in agreement then. The ideal candidate must be one that avoids the animal facilities, the glasshouses, and the broken tools.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
