55,3,1,talk,Servas,,"We have our candidates. Looking at them, the Microbiome Atlas seems the most harmonious, as it avoids the glasshouses and the technician shortage.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Sakura,,The Atlas sounds great! It doesn't need the expensive animal units or the full glasshouses. It's a safe bet for the budget!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. The Atlas is a catalogue project. My research shows those are the only ones that actually deliver lasting value.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"It's the only one that makes sense. Protein Folding needs spectroscopy, and the others need glasshouses or animals. The Atlas is the way.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Minako,,I concur. The Atlas avoids the overcapacity of the glasshouses and the high costs of the vivarium. It is the most sustainable choice.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Servas,,"It is a rare pleasure to see such unity. We have balanced the human, financial, and structural realities of our agency.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Sakura,,Yay! I'm so happy we all agree! Let's give the grant to the Atlas!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I feel... more confident in this choice because the data supports it. I am ready to vote.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"No more delays, no more broken machines. Let's just do it.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Minako,,The logic is sound and the risks are minimized. I am ready.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Servas,,I cast my vote for the Microbiome Atlas.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I vote for the Microbiome Atlas!,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
